  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nDry and warm conditions continue into Thursday, with subtropical\nmoisture remaining south and east of the area. Some showers and\nthunderstorms may form in the central ID mountains and south \nalong the NV border Thursday afternoon. An upper level trough\nfrom the Gulf of Alaska will move southeast into the Pacific NW\nlate Thursday. A cold front moves through southeast OR and\nsouthwest ID on Friday with cooler and unsettled conditions \npossible Saturday and Sunday. Still significant model \ndifferences in the positioning of this trough, but wetting rains\npossible next weekend and much cooler temperatures as much as \n10-20 degrees below normal.",
